{"tool_name":"cafe-r","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"cafe-r","home":"http://microbiology.se/software/cafe/","license":"MIT","summary":"A software suite for analysis of paired-sample transposon insertion sequencing data.\n\nCAFE \u2013 Coefficient-based Analysis of Fitness by read Enrichments.\n\nThe R package part of CAFE can be installed in R using the devtools package and: install_github(\"bengtssonpalme/cafe\").","addition_date":"2021-03-19T08:36:24Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:38:11.371770Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:cafe-r","credit":[{"email":"johan.bengtsson-palme@microbiology.se","name":"Johan Bengtsson-Palme","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3501"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]}],"name":"CAFE-R","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btaa1086","metadata":{"abstract":"Sequencing of transposon insertion libraries is used to determine the relative fitness of individual mutants at a large scale. However, there is a lack of tools for specifically analyzing data from such experiments with paired sample designs. Here, we introduce CAFE - Coefficient-based Analysis of Fitness by read Enrichment - a software package that can analyze data from paired transposon mutant sequencing experiments, generate fitness coefficients for each gene and condition and perform appropriate statistical testing on these fitness coefficients.","authors":[{"name":"Abramova A."},{"name":"Bengtsson-Palme J."},{"name":"Burman E."},{"name":"Kunche H."},{"name":"Osinska A."}],"citationCount":5,"date":"2021-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"CAFE: a software suite for analysis of paired-sample transposon insertion sequencing data"},"pmcid":"PMC8034522","pmid":"3339398